---
id: intent_router.route
description: Decides whether a staff message clearly asks to start an expert workflow, and which one.
owner: eng
component: orchestrator_services
overridable: true
output: json
schema:
  type: object
  required: [should_route_to_expert]
  properties:
    should_route_to_expert: {type: boolean}
    confidence: {type: number}
    command: {type: string}
    packet_type: {type: string}
    key_entity: {type: string}
    args: {type: string}
    latitude: {type: string}
    longitude: {type: string}
    raw_request: {type: string}
sections: []
variables: [now_str, user_input_repr]
access:
  view: [ops, eng]
  edit: []
  publish: []
---
TODAY'S DATE AND TIME: {{now_str}}

Decide whether this staff message is clearly asking to start an expert workflow.
Only route when the intent is explicit. Do not route ordinary questions, status checks, or vague requests.

Supported expert workflows:
- /lpp -> light_preliminary_package: create or generate a Light Preliminary Package for a named site or GPS coordinates.

Message: {{user_input_repr}}

Return only JSON with this shape:
{"should_route_to_expert": false, "confidence": 0.0, "command": "/lpp", "packet_type": "light_preliminary_package", "key_entity": "site name or coordinate pair, if present", "args": "slash-command arguments, if present", "latitude": "decimal latitude, if present", "longitude": "decimal longitude, if present", "raw_request": "original user message"}
